cast: zara

== room | NIGHT · ZARA'S ROOM | cozy student bedroom at night with fairy lights, books and a big window | phone
zara (worried): Quddus, help. My statement of purpose starts with, since I was born, I have always loved education.
quddus (talk): Zara... the committee reads hundreds of those. Delete it. Gently.
zara (shrug): Then what do I write? My whole life story?
quddus (talk): No. A statement of purpose answers three questions: what you want to study, why you're ready, and where it will take you.

== library | NEXT DAY · LIBRARY | bright modern library with wooden shelves, study tables and big windows | cafe
zara (think): Okay. Give me the structure.
quddus (point): Open with a real moment that started your interest. Then show what you've done: projects, work, research, results.
> 1f4dd | SOP STRUCTURE | 1f4a1 A real moment, not a quote | 1f4c8 What you've done, with results | 1f3db Why THIS program | 1f680 Your goal after it
zara (talk): And why this program?
quddus (talk): Name specific courses, professors or labs, and connect them to your goals. Copy and paste is easy to spot.
zara (worried): So I can't send the same statement to ten schools?
quddus (thumbs): Keep your story, but change the why this program part for each one. And keep within their word limit.
zara (cheer): New first line: the day our village lost power for a week, I decided to study renewable energy.
quddus (cheer): Now THAT makes people keep reading!
